  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts. It typechecks, but I couldn't run `vite build` or load the scene in a browser, so none of the rendering has been viewed.\n\n- **Island:** a flat-shaded heightfield with sand, grass, rock and snow colours by height. It also has instanced two-tier cone trees with trunks, and rocks. Everything is generated in code, with no model files.\n- **Water:** a custom GLSL wave mesh with three animated waves, fresnel, a sun or moon glint, a shallow shore tint and shore foam. Its colours follow the day/night value.\n- **Day/night:** a full cycle takes 20 seconds. `sky.preetham` and the `sun` and `moon` directional lights move each frame, and the fog colour shifts with the time of day. A hemisphere light and the moon keep the scene from going black at night. `?hour=` freezes the clock.\n- **Camera:** it sits above the water at about 17 m and orbits slowly around the island, set each frame with `app.camera.setPose`.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set on a `requestAnimationFrame` after `app.ready()`.\n\nI couldn't confirm that `app.camera?.setPose` actually moves the camera at runtime, so the orbit is unchecked. If it does nothing, the camera stays at its starting position, which still frames the island.\n\n",
